    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist: Multi-Node Language-Model Serving System\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or replicated sharding) behaves **identically, correctly, and measurably** across all nodes. It is written to catch the failure modes that single-node testing misses: silent rank divergence, partial participation, dropped or double-counted requests, and timing artifacts from synchronization.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal: Prove every node is running the same logical system.**\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact hash**: Record SHA-256 of model weights, tokenizer files, and config files on every node. All hashes must match. Verify *after* loading, not just at rest \u2014 catch cases where a node falls back to a cached or default checkpoint.\n- [ ] **Effective config dump**: Each rank must emit its *resolved* configuration (post-merge of defaults, env vars, CLI flags, config files) at startup. Diff these dumps across ranks; they must be byte-identical except for explicitly rank-dependent fields (rank ID, local device index, local world size).\n- [ ] **Rank-dependent field audit**: Enumerate every field allowed to differ per rank (e.g., `rank`, `local_rank`, `device_uuid`, `local_batch_size`). Anything outside this allowlist differing is a hard failure.\n- [ ] **Version pinning**: Log versions of the inference engine, framework (vLLM/TensorRT-LLM/DeepSpeed etc.), CUDA/ROCm, NCCL/HCCL, driver, and container image digest per node. Mismatched NCCL versions are a classic silent-participation cause.\n- [ ] **Sharding plan verification**: For each weight tensor, log its sharding strategy (TP/PP/EP dimension, shard index, expected shape) per rank. Validate that concatenating shards along the declared",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
